* `Workspace.Types.Classes` — `InF11` (the class `F₁₁` of §1);
* `Workspace.Types.Decompositions` — `AdmitsBalancedSkewPartition`.

Encoding conventions (see `paper/spec/CONVENTIONS.md`):

* a path of the paper is an *induced* subgraph, given by the list `p : List V` of
  its vertices in order; the paper's `p₁-⋯-pₙ` therefore has `n = p.length`
  vertices and length `pathLength p = n - 1`, its interior `p₂,…,pₙ₋₁` is
  `SPGT.interior p` (always written qualified — a bare `interior` is Mathlib's
  topological one), and `V(P)` is `{w : V | w ∈ p}` (so *"`z ∉ V(P)`"* is
  `z ∉ p`);
* the ends `p₁, pₙ` and the second vertex `p₂` are pinned down by the total
  functions `p.head?`, `p.getLast?`, `p.tail.head?` (no `getElem` bounds needed);
* *"an edge of `P`"*: since `P` is induced, the edges of `P` are exactly the
  adjacent pairs of vertices of `p`, so *"some edge of `P` is `X`-complete"* is
  `∃ a ∈ p, ∃ b ∈ p, EdgeComplete G X a b` (`EdgeComplete` already contains
  `G.Adj a b`);
* a hole is the list of its vertices in cyclic order, with length `holeLength`;
* *"`X` is complete to `Y`"* is `Complete G X Y`, *"`v` is `X`-complete"* is
  `VertexComplete G v X`;
* *"`G` is complete"* means every two distinct vertices of `G` are adjacent, and
  *"`G` is bipartite"* is Mathlib's `SimpleGraph.IsBipartite` (= `Colorable 2`).
